INT. BOWLING ALLEY - LEAGUE NIGHT

Neon pins. Fryer smell. Scoreboards flicker.

Lane Six. BIG ARNOLD KESSLER (50s) lifts a ball. His rival WILHELMINA "MINNIE" TRAN (50s) crosses her arms behind him. At the counter, the owner DEACON FOLEY (60s) polishes shoes. At a corner table, teenager POPPY ESTRADA (16) keeps score, chewing a straw.

He rolls. Strike. She doesn't clap. He turns. She smirks.

She steps up, rolls. Gutter. He laughs. She glares.

Deacon looks at the clock. Poppy looks at her phone.

ARNOLD
Tough break.

MINNIE
Wait your turn.

He picks a ball. So does she. They reach for the same one. Their hands collide. Both pull back.

DEACON
Folks, there's a rack of them.

Arnold shrugs and takes another. Minnie takes the first, grips it, and rolls. Strike. She turns and bows, slowly. He nods, grudging.

POPPY
That's two-forty to two-thirty-eight.

Neither of them breathes. Then both start toward the scoreboard at once, shoving past each other, until Deacon steps between them with both palms out.
